# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
# EVERY VARIANT BUILD A `verify-` SCRIPT LEAVES BEHIND, BY GLOB (KAN-522).
#
# This was four hand-maintained patterns — `dist-unfixed/` (the baseline
# verify-mcp-runtime-validation.mjs compares against), `dist-guardless-*/` (the
# guard-removed copy verify-board-reconciler-guard.mjs builds), and
# `dist-kan342-red-*/` (verify-absence-is-not-intent.mjs's red drive) — and the
# comment on the last one recorded that KAN-368 added it after `git add -A`
# swept 58 of its files into a commit, the two before it existing "because that
# had already happened twice."
#
# It has now happened twice more, on the same day, to two agents independently:
# `dist-kan343-nohealth-*` and `dist-kan343-unscoped-*` reached #232 and #233 —
# 130 files and 82,764 insertions on this branch — behind every required check
# green, because nothing in the gate has an opinion about build output entering
# the repository (filed as KAN-531; this glob is not that fix).
#
# FOUR OCCURRENCES IS THE ENUMERATION FAILING, NOT FOUR ACCIDENTS. A list that
# must be extended by hand for every ticket that builds a variant is a list that
# is wrong for exactly as long as it takes somebody to notice, and the noticing
# has cost two PRs a review cycle. The glob cannot be behind.
#
# Control before landing it: `git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main | grep -E
# '(^|/)dist-'` returns nothing, so no tracked file becomes newly ignored — and
# the same grep against this branch returns its 130, so the check can find them
# when they are there.
dist-*/

# Logs
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
